# The other half of `spec/grammar.md:34`: a newline still ends a statement when no expression is
# pending, and consecutive newlines are a single separator. A `-` glued to a numeral is a negative
# `number` literal (`spec/grammar.md:60`), so it opens a new statement instead of continuing the
# line above — the guard that keeps issue #933's fix from swallowing the statement after it.
print 1
print 2


print 3
-5
print [4
-6]
